<div class="tale-introduction"><p class="eyebrow">FROM AYODHYA TO CHITRAKUTA</p><p>This original English retelling follows selected episodes in the <strong>Valmiki Ramayana’s Ayodhya Kanda</strong>, from the planned consecration to the forest dwelling at Chitrakuta. It tells the beginning of the fourteen-year exile. Extended conversations, rituals and descriptions are condensed.</p></div>
<section class="story-characters" aria-labelledby="characters-title"><p class="eyebrow">MEET THE CHARACTERS</p><h2 id="characters-title">Characters in this story</h2><dl><div><dt>Rama</dt><dd>Dasharatha’s son, who accepts the forest exile.</dd></div><div><dt>Sita</dt><dd>Rama’s wife, who insists on sharing his journey.</dd></div><div><dt>Lakshmana</dt><dd>Rama’s brother, who chooses to accompany and serve him.</dd></div><div><dt>Dasharatha</dt><dd>King of Ayodhya, bound by his promised boons.</dd></div><div><dt>Kaikeyi</dt><dd>Bharata’s mother, who claims the two boons.</dd></div><div><dt>Sumantra</dt><dd>The charioteer who takes the family out of Ayodhya.</dd></div><div><dt>Guha</dt><dd>The ally who helps arrange the Ganga crossing.</dd></div><div><dt>Bharadwaja</dt><dd>The sage who welcomes them and recommends Chitrakuta.</dd></div></dl></section>
